{
  "summary": "User James O'Connor (Operations, Warehouse Supervisor, user_id 8) reports two issues: (1) his desktop BL-DT-0108 has no network connection, (2) floor 2 printer BL-PR-FL2 is down. Findings: BL-DT-0108 is offline, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:05 UTC, no warnings, disk fine. BL-PR-FL2 is offline, last check-in 2026-10-10 22:05 UTC, no warnings. Account is active and healthy (not locked or blocked). Two wired devices, probably on the same floor, going offline within a few hours of each other could mean a shared network fault (switch, port, or floor network segment), not two separate device faults. No KB covers a wired desktop losing network. KB-014 is Wi-Fi-only and says to escalate if the office network is down for several people. KB-022 printer steps (clear errors, power cycle, check cable or link light) have been passed to the user to try. Still needed: check the floor 2 switch or network segment, find out whether other floor 2 users or devices are affected, and send onsite help if needed. Priority may need raising if the floor is affected.",
  "reason": "Desktop and printer both offline. Possible shared network fault, and no KB covers a wired desktop with no network."
}
